From 51c1a32cd78cfb0a14087e34dfcc06be30928a0e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 23:41:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Project CED global KV on local rows before gathering its
 latent

Upstream base: 19f2c20ed4d64ae22bd009ceacadd85e2a81e354.
Integration base: 6d4e49d1cdbb6513819e47145e0e52fdab327b6b.
Immediate base: 2b320049a5df8e62e1b3ee70f53304d6d55a15e3.

Build ratio-one global KV from row-local BF16 projections and gather the
512-column result, retaining every encoder row for norm, cache and index
writes. Gather normalized query rows only for the selected replay. Count
padding and TP3's additional latent gather before choosing the sparse path.

Aligned TP retains one full compressor weight before memory profiling;
TP3 already holds it. Decode keeps its original weight and kernels. The
prefill kernel uses the original column shard's K partition and block
ordering even when a local row slice crosses the decode-size boundary.

Quality: no checkpoint quantization, norm change, floating collective sum,
attention backend change or replay-selection change. Native equality is a
qualification requirement, not inferred from the CPU arithmetic stand-ins.

Tests: 151 CPU checks pass, one GPU test skipped. Both BF16 projection
shapes compile offline for SM121a with the deployed five blocked K parts.
Added TP3/TP4 native projection and rank-order mHC row-invariance checks
remain pending hardware. No serving throughput gain is claimed.
Upstream status: experimental alternative for source-fork review; unpromoted.
